# Nissan GTR Auto ERP — Global Laws
# These rules apply to ALL agents across ALL lanes unless a path-specific
# .cursor/rules/*.mdc file provides a more specific override.

## Hard Exclusions (NEVER implement, scaffold, or leave TODOs for)

- NO ZIMRA integration of any kind. No FDMS connections, no fiscalisation QR codes,
  no ZIMRA payload compilation, no mTLS fiscal device logic in checkout, invoicing, or receipts.
  Invoices are standard tax-agnostic documents.
- NO tax calculation or tax-authority integration in Payroll. No PAYE, no NSSA POBS/APWCS/ZIMDEF,
  no statutory remittance forms (P4/P4A), no tax brackets. Payroll computes gross pay from
  attendance/hours/salary structure only, with manual/custom deduction line items.

## Bridge-First Rule

Any camera, QR, Bluetooth printer, biometric sensor, or GPS access MUST go through an isolated
native bridge module under `bridges/`, never a browser/WebView API. No HTML5 QR scanning libraries.
Route hardware work to @hardware_mobile_agent.

## Supabase RLS Mandate

Every table gets Row Level Security policies before being considered "done". No table ships open.
New migrations must include RLS policies in the same migration file.

## Multi-Currency Awareness

All money fields carry an explicit currency (`USD` | `ZIG`). Where converted, store the exchange rate
applied at time of transaction. Never silently assume USD.

## Ledger Immutability

Financial ledger entries are append-only. Corrections happen via reversing/contra entries, never
edits or deletes. Every entry stores who posted it and when.

## Quarantine Returns Protocol

Faulty-item returns debit "Sales Returns & Allowances" (contra-revenue) and credit the customer's
AR/store credit. The returned SKU goes to a Quarantine warehouse — never a direct exchange.

## Core Charge Handling

Parent-child cart schema splits deposit/core-charge lines from the physical part's price at cart
insertion. Revenue and COGS must remain accurate.

## Token & Context Discipline

1. Load skills only when their trigger condition matches the current task.
2. Stay within your agent lane (see rufler.yaml). Cross-lane work routes to named agents.
3. Propose targeted diffs/patches for existing files — full-file output only for new files.
4. Check claude-mem and `docs/decisions/` for prior schema decisions before re-deriving from blueprints.
5. Reference relevant sub-sections of long specs rather than re-quoting entire sections.
6. Batch related migrations, rule updates, or skill edits into single passes.
7. Heavy design skills (ui-ux-pro-max, brand, slides, design-system) are explicit-invoke only — never load them for non-UI tasks.
8. Prefer progressive memory search (index → timeline → details) over dumping full histories into context.
9. See `/token-discipline` and `.cursor/rules/session_discipline.mdc`.

## Code Conventions

- Match existing naming, types, and abstractions in the surrounding code.
- Minimize scope — simplest correct diff wins.
- Shared business logic lives in `packages/shared/`, never duplicated per app.
- Data pipeline (`data-pipeline/`) is independent of client app builds.
- Supabase migrations are version-controlled, never dashboard-only.
